---
title: SSD1306 - 128x64 OLED over I2C
---
%% NO DOCUMENTED PINS - the driver takes an I2C bus and an address.
%% PA8 / PC9 are already I2C3_SCL / I2C3_SDA in project.ioc.
%% Address is 0x3C on most modules, 0x3D if the board's address jumper is moved.
%% Nearly all SSD1306 breakouts include pull-ups and a regulator, so VCC can be
%% 3.3 V or 5 V - but the logic pins are then 3.3 V, which suits this board.
%% Only 4 wires: there is no reset or chip-select in the I2C variant.
flowchart LR
    subgraph MCU["STM32F429I-DISC1"]
        SCL["PA8 - I2C3_SCL"]
        SDA["PC9 - I2C3_SDA"]
        V33["3V3"]
        GND["GND"]
    end

    PU["4.7k pull-ups - usually already fitted on the module"]

    subgraph OLED["SSD1306 128x64 module - addr 0x3C"]
        oV["VCC"]
        oG["GND"]
        oSCL["SCL"]
        oSDA["SDA"]
    end

    PU --- SCL
    PU --- SDA
    SCL --> oSCL
    SDA <--> oSDA
    V33 --- oV
    GND --- oG
